      ⍝ Equal and not-equal compare characters as well as numbers. Every
      ⍝ other scalar function takes numbers only.
      W←'MISSISSIPPI'
      W='S'
0 0 1 1 0 1 1 0 0 0 0
      ⍝ How many of a letter, and where they are.
      +/W='S'
4
      (W='S')/⍳⍴W
3 4 6 7
      ⍝ Everything but the letter.
      (W≠'S')/W
MIIIPPI
